<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<style xmlns="http://purl.org/net/xbiblio/csl" class="in-text" version="1.0" demote-non-dropping-particle="sort-only" initialize-with-hyphen="false" default-locale="en-US">
  <!--
    Why not the standard NLM style (nlm-citation-sequence), which NIH suggests
    and this style is based on? Used in Zotero for an NIH application, NLM:
    - prints the DOI of every item that has one, and for everything but
      journal articles "[cited date]. Available from: URL" too; pasted from
      Zotero, each one is a live link. NIH allows hyperlinks and
      URLs only where a funding opportunity or form instructions say so
      (SF424 application guide, "Format Attachments"), and grants offices flag
      links, even ones inside the document.
    - shortens author lists of seven or more to six names and "et al." NIH's
      instructions have asked for all authors, in the order on the paper.
    - doesn't mark preprints: even saved as Zotero's Preprint type, it prints
      "[Internet]. medRxiv; 2024. Available from: URL doi:...", with the year
      only. NIH asks for preprints to be cited with "[Preprint]", a date for
      the version and the DOI (NOT-OD-17-050).
    (NLM does print the PMCID, as "PubMed Central PMCID", which the NIH Public
    Access Policy requires for the applicant's NIH-supported papers; this
    style keeps it, as plain "PMCID: PMC...".)

    So this style prints no URL or access date anywhere, lists every author,
    prints the PMCID from the item's Extra field, and gives preprints the
    server, "[Preprint]", the posting date and the DOI (or, with no DOI, the
    Archive ID, such as an arXiv number). NIH's own example cites the DOI as a
    doi.org web address with a [cited] date; this style prints it as
    "doi: 10..." instead, so there is no URL.

    Save each preprint in Zotero as item type Preprint, with Repository (the
    server) and Date (the posting date of the version cited). A preprint
    saved as a Journal Article prints with no "[Preprint]" and no DOI.

    WARNING: links. Whether that DOI is a link depends on how the references
    get into the document, not on the style (tested with this style and NLM
    in Zotero 10.0.7, see docs/zotero-link-test-plan.md; steps in the README):
    - Word, inserted with the Zotero plugin: no links, the DOI is plain text
      (tested on Windows; Mac not tested).
    - Google Docs, inserted with the plugin: every citation and the whole
      bibliography link to zotero.org. Run Zotero > Unlink Citations in a
      final copy, then export that copy.
    - Pasted from Quick Copy: DOIs link to doi.org and URLs to themselves,
      in either editor, and unlinking leaves them. Create Bibliography wasn't
      tested but works the same way in Zotero's code. Never paste a
      bibliography.
    Then check the final PDF for links: a reference pasted or typed by hand
    can bring one in.

    A paper within three months of publication may be cited with its NIHMS ID
    instead of a PMCID; Zotero has no field for it, so add it by hand (see the
    README). Check the current SF424 guide and your funding opportunity before
    each submission.
  -->
  <info>
    <title>National Institutes of Health Grant Proposal</title>
    <title-short>NIH Grant</title-short>
    <id>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vlmurthylab/csl-styles/main/nih-grant-proposal.csl</id>
    <link href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vlmurthylab/csl-styles/main/nih-grant-proposal.csl" rel="self"/>
    <link href="http://www.zotero.org/styles/nlm-citation-sequence" rel="template"/>
    <link href="https://grants.nih.gov/grants-process/write-application/how-to-apply-application-guide/format-attachments" rel="documentation"/>
    <link href="https://grants.nih.gov/grants/guide/notice-files/NOT-OD-17-050.html" rel="documentation"/>
    <link href="https://grants.nih.gov/grants/policy/nihgps/html5/section_8/8.2.2_nih_public_access_policy.htm" rel="documentation"/>
    <author>
      <name>Venkatesh Murthy</name>
    </author>
    <contributor>
      <name>Michael Berkowitz</name>
    </contributor>
    <contributor>
      <name>Sebastian Karcher</name>
    </contributor>
    <contributor>
      <name>Matt Tracy</name>
    </contributor>
    <category citation-format="numeric"/>
    <category field="medicine"/>
    <summary>NLM-style numbered references for NIH applications, which allow no hyperlinks: no URLs or access dates, and a DOI only for preprints, where NIH asks for it. Every author is listed, and a PMCID is printed as plain text when the item has one. WARNING: insert references with the Zotero plugin and never paste a bibliography (pasted DOIs are live links); in Google Docs, unlink citations in a final copy before exporting.</summary>
    <updated>2026-11-01T20:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <rights license="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 License</rights>
  </info>
  <locale xml:lang="en">
    <terms>
      <term name="presented at">presented at</term>
      <term name="section" form="short">sect.</term>
    </terms>
  </locale>
  <macro name="author">
    <names variable="author" suffix=". ">
      <name sort-separator=" " initialize-with="" name-as-sort-order="all" delimiter=", " delimiter-precedes-last="always"/>
      <label form="long" prefix=", "/>
      <substitute>
        <names variable="editor"/>
      </substitute>
    </names>
  </macro>
  <!-- "In: Editor A, editor. Book title" for chapters and conference papers;
       "In:" stays even with no editor, so the book isn't read as the author's -->
  <macro name="editor">
    <group delimiter=": ">
      <choose>
        <if type="chapter paper-conference" match="any">
          <text term="in" text-case="capitalize-first"/>
        </if>
      </choose>
      <group delimiter=" ">
        <names variable="editor" suffix=".">
          <name sort-separator=" " initialize-with="" name-as-sort-order="all" delimiter=", " delimiter-precedes-last="always"/>
          <label form="long" prefix=", "/>
        </names>
        <text variable="container-title"/>
      </group>
    </group>
  </macro>
  <macro name="publisher">
    <group delimiter=": " suffix=";">
      <choose>
        <if type="thesis">
          <text variable="publisher-place" prefix="[" suffix="]"/>
        </if>
        <else-if type="speech"/>
        <else>
          <text variable="publisher-place"/>
        </else>
      </choose>
      <text variable="publisher"/>
    </group>
  </macro>
  <macro name="journal-title">
    <choose>
      <if type="article-journal article-magazine" match="any">
        <group suffix=". ">
          <text variable="container-title" form="short" font-style="italic" strip-periods="true"/>
        </group>
      </if>
      <else>
        <text variable="container-title" suffix=". " form="short"/>
      </else>
    </choose>
  </macro>
  <macro name="title">
    <text variable="title"/>
    <choose>
      <if type="article-journal article-magazine chapter paper-conference article-newspaper" match="none">
        <text macro="edition" prefix=". "/>
      </if>
    </choose>
    <choose>
      <if type="thesis">
        <text variable="genre" prefix=" [" suffix="]"/>
      </if>
    </choose>
  </macro>
  <macro name="edition">
    <choose>
      <if is-numeric="edition">
        <group delimiter=" ">
          <number variable="edition" form="ordinal"/>
          <text term="edition" form="short"/>
        </group>
      </if>
      <else>
        <text variable="edition" suffix="."/>
      </else>
    </choose>
  </macro>
  <macro name="report-details">
    <choose>
      <if type="report">
        <text variable="number" prefix="Report No.: "/>
      </if>
    </choose>
  </macro>
  <citation collapse="citation-number">
    <sort>
      <key variable="citation-number"/>
    </sort>
    <layout vertical-align="sup" delimiter=",">
      <text variable="citation-number"/>
    </layout>
  </citation>
  <bibliography second-field-align="flush">
    <layout>
      <text variable="citation-number" suffix=". "/>
      <text macro="author"/>
      <text macro="title" suffix=". "/>
      <choose>
        <if type="bill book graphic legal_case legislation motion_picture report song thesis" match="any">
          <group prefix=" " delimiter=" ">
            <text macro="publisher"/>
            <date variable="issued" suffix=".">
              <date-part name="year"/>
            </date>
          </group>
          <text macro="report-details" prefix=" " suffix="."/>
        </if>
        <else-if type="chapter paper-conference" match="any">
          <!-- NLM: In: Editor A, editor. Book title. Place: Publisher; Year. p. 1-20. -->
          <text macro="editor" prefix=" " suffix="."/>
          <group prefix=" " delimiter=" ">
            <text macro="publisher"/>
            <date variable="issued" suffix=".">
              <date-part name="year"/>
            </date>
          </group>
          <text variable="page" prefix=" p. " suffix="."/>
        </else-if>
        <else>
          <choose>
            <if type="article">
              <!-- Preprint, as NIH asks (NOT-OD-17-050): the server's name (Zotero's
                   Repository field), "[Preprint]", the posting date (which identifies
                   the version) and the DOI. This is the only DOI the style prints, and
                   never a URL. Inserted with the Word plugin the DOI is plain text;
                   pasted from Quick Copy it becomes a link (see the warning at
                   the top and the README). -->
              <choose>
                <if variable="publisher">
                  <text variable="publisher" prefix=" " suffix=" "/>
                </if>
                <else-if variable="archive">
                  <text variable="archive" prefix=" " suffix=" "/>
                </else-if>
              </choose>
              <text value="[Preprint]."/>
              <group prefix=" " delimiter=" ">
                <date variable="issued" delimiter=" " suffix=".">
                  <date-part name="year"/>
                  <date-part name="month" form="short" strip-periods="true"/>
                  <date-part name="day"/>
                </date>
                <choose>
                  <if variable="DOI">
                    <text variable="DOI" prefix="doi: " suffix="."/>
                  </if>
                  <else>
                    <!-- No DOI: the Archive ID (an arXiv number), as plain text -->
                    <text variable="number" suffix="."/>
                  </else>
                </choose>
              </group>
            </if>
            <else>
              <text macro="journal-title"/>
              <!-- "2021;12:100-110." or just "2021." (no stray semicolon) -->
              <group delimiter=";" suffix=".">
                <date variable="issued">
                  <date-part name="year"/>
                </date>
                <group>
                  <text variable="volume"/>
                  <text variable="page" prefix=":"/>
                </group>
              </group>
            </else>
          </choose>
          <!-- NIH public access policy: PMCID as plain text, only if the item has one -->
          <text variable="PMCID" prefix=" PMCID: " suffix="."/>
        </else>
      </choose>
    </layout>
  </bibliography>
</style>
